h Manson (Out)\n\n🏒 Oilers @ Devils · 7:30 PM ET\n📍 bet105: Devils -1.5 (+164) · O/U 6 · ML Oilers +135 / Devils -151\n📊 Oilers 9-3, O/U 6-6, last 5 LLWWW | Devils 8-4, O/U 7-5, last 5 WWWLW\n🛌 Oilers 1 day rest · Devils 3 days rest\n🥅 Oilers: Tristan Jarry · Devils: Connor Hellebuyck\n\n🏒 Hurricanes @ Predators · 8 PM ET\n📍 bet105: Predators +1.5 (-145) · O/U 6.5 · ML Hurricanes -196 / Predators +173\n📊 Hurricanes 11-2, O/U 6-7, last 5 LWWWW | Predators 4-8, O/U 8-4, last 5 LWLLW\n🛌 Hurricanes 1 day rest · Predators 2 days rest\n🥅 Hurricanes: Pyotr Kochetkov · Predators: Juuse Saros\n🚑 Hurricanes Alexander Nikishin (Out)\n\n🏒 Ducks @ Canucks · 9 PM ET\n📍 bet105: Canucks +1.5 (-181) · O/U 6.5 · ML Ducks -154 / Canucks +137\n📊 Ducks 4-8, O/U 6-6, last 5 LWLLW | Canucks 1-11, O/U 5-7, last 5 LLWLL\n🛌 Ducks 1 day rest · Canucks 2 days rest\n🥅 Ducks: Lukas Dostal · Canucks: Leevi Merilainen\n\nRecords vs closing lines, this season. Lines can move. Data, not picks. Who are you on tonight? 👇"},"text":"🗓️ TODAY'S BOARD AT BET105\n11 games: 🏒 11 NHL. Every line, every stat. Data, not picks.\n\n⚡ QUICK HITS\n🏒 Biggest favorite: Lightning -272\n🛌 On a back-to-back: 🏒 Red Wings, 🏒 Golden Knights, 🏒 Avalanche\n\n🏒 NHL TONIGHT\n\n🏒 Mammoth @ Maple Leafs · 7 PM ET\n📍 bet105: Maple https://t.co/e14bjxARgt","url":"https://x.com/bet_105/status/2117652707485851769"},{"author_id":"367857312","created_at":"2026-11-03T14:29:58.000Z","edit_history_tweet_ids":["2117625336863092936"],"id":"2117625336863092936","note_tweet":{"entities":{"hashtags":[{"end":14,"start":5,"tag":"NJDevils"},{"end":58,"start":45,"tag":"LetsGoOilers"}],"mentions":[{"end":38,"id":"2095889771327324163","start":24,"username":"TheDevilsEdge"}]},"text":"It's #NJDevils game day @TheDevilsEdge \n\nThe #LetsGoOilers come to town 1st in the Western Conference with an 11-2-2 record. They are 2nd in the NHL in GF/G. 3rd in PP%.\n\nConnor McDavid is on pace for 218 points this season (would be an NHL record). He has at least 1 assist in every game so far this season. McDavid/Draisaitl/Bouchard's 93 combined points is more than 4 NHL teams cumulative total.\n\nThe Devils will try to slow them down. They are top heavy. The Devils can roll 4 lines and NJ will have the last change tonight at home. Tristan Jarry is 39th in the NHL (> 5GP) in GSAx/60 at -0.4.\n\nNJ is 5th in the NHL in xGF/60 at 5v5 (2.9). The Oilers are 26th (2.3). Stay out the box. Tread water against 97. Let the depth shine. Get pucks to the net."},"text":"It's #NJDevils game day @TheDevilsEdge \n\nThe #LetsGoOilers come to town 1st in the Western Conference with an 11-2-2 record. They are 2nd in the NHL in GF/G. 3rd in PP%.\n\nConnor McDavid is on pace for 218 points this season (would be an NHL record). He has at least 1 assist in https://t.co/P5tSrNk8Ib","url":"https://x.com/KeithKavJr/status/2117625336863092936"},{"author_id":"267194006","created_at":"2026-11-03T19:52:31.000Z","edit_history_tweet_ids":["2117706508570124313"],"id":"2117706508570124313","note_tweet":{"text":"𝑵𝑯𝑳 𝑷𝒍𝒂𝒚𝒔 𝒕𝒐𝒅𝒂𝒚, 𝑷𝒍𝒆𝒂𝒔𝒆 𝑹𝒆𝒂𝒅:\nPlease don't go big on any of these unless you see reasons otherwise. These are all pretty much value-lean shots. I'm hoping to catch some bad lines, but I know these could all lose. This includes my Jets collaboration play. They are all going to be half a unit.\n\n𝐑𝐄𝐃 𝐖𝐈𝐍𝐆𝐒 𝐌𝐋 +𝟐𝟑𝟑 (𝟎.𝟓𝐮)\nI think there's an understanding that an underdog team like Detroit isn't necessarily expected to beat both Florida teams on back-to-back nights. That said, I really like what Todd McLellan has done with this Wings team this year. They're playing with a competitive edge, and watching yesterday's game, you could see how much fight this group has. Even when the Panthers were launching a full-on assault offensively, Detroit just kept pushing and never really backed down.\n\nI also think the Detroit core is seriously underrated. DeBrincat, Raymond, Seider, and some of the younger guys like Finnie and MBN don't get nearly enough recognition, largely because this team still doesn't get much respect. The reality is that Detroit keeps finding ways to win games nobody expects them to, and I think tonight could be another one of those situations.\n\nI'm also not too concerned about the back-to-back fatigue here. The travel wasn't particularly demanding, and I actually think the Wings could feed off yesterday's performance rather than come out looking exhausted or out of sync. They seem to have a bit of momentum behind them right now.\n\nOn the other side, the Kucherov situation can't be helping Tampa's locker room. Obviously, this is just speculation, but I wouldn't be surprised if some chemistry starts to erode the longer this situation drags on without a trade.\n\nAll things considered, I think Detroit is worth a serious look tonight.\n\n𝐌𝐚𝐦𝐦𝐨𝐭𝐡/𝐌𝐚𝐩𝐥𝐞 𝐋𝐞𝐚𝐟𝐬 𝐔𝐍𝐃𝐄𝐑 𝟕 (𝟎.𝟓𝐮)\nThis isn't a great value play, but some books have gone as high as 7, which I think is pretty high. At -130s to -140s, though, I don't think it's worth more than half a unit. Toronto just snapped a 5-game OVER streak, and I think things slow down for them a bit. Utah is coming off two high-scoring games, but giving up 6 goals to the Flyers should be enough to get them to tighten things up against a potent offense. Plus, I don't see either team wanting another run-and-gun game like their recent meeting.\n\n𝐅𝐋𝐘𝐄𝐑𝐒 𝐌𝐋 +𝟏𝟔𝟐 (𝟎.𝟓𝐮)\nPhilly has been a bit unpredictable since bouncing back from that brutal 7-game start to the season, but I think the books are putting a little too much weight on those early struggles. Combine that with Minnesota being elite and looking like the contender everyone expected them to be, and I think we've ended up with a pretty lopsided line.\n\nOne thing that I don't think is getting nearly enough attention is the massive boost Philly just got with Cam York, Travis Konecny, and Owen Tippett returning. We already saw the impact in their last game. This team now has three lines with legitimate offensive firepower and looks much more complete defensively, which should only make things easier on a goaltending group that's already been overall fine.\n\nCates has also started to find his game after a slow start, Zegras and Michkov look like they're already in midseason form, and Martone is starting to come around as well. There's a lot to like here, and this is a team that should be capable of hanging with just about anyone.\n\nMinnesota is absolutely legit, and when they're playing their best, they can beat anyone too. But that's kind of my point: I see these teams as much closer than the odds suggest. At +162, Philly feels like a coin-flip type of play to me.\n\n𝐎𝐈𝐋𝐄𝐑𝐒 𝐌𝐋 +𝟏𝟑𝟖 (𝟎.𝟓𝐮)\nCould this be a trap? Maybe, but I'm not fully buying it. I think two things are going on with this line:\n\n1. Edmonton's injury impact is being way overblown.\n\n2.NJ is a contender that's still riding the Hellebuyck hype, and they're playing at home.\n\nSure, it sucks that Hyman is out again, and the Oilers' goaltending concerns are valid. But I really think Babcock's system is overriding those factors. The game plan is pretty simple: everyone outside the big three just needs to make life easier for whoever's in net and take turns chipping in offensively. \n\nAs long as the big three (McDavid, Draisaitl, and Bouchard) are in the lineup and everyone else sticks to their role, Edmonton can beat anyone, even with an AHL goalie in the Oilers net (they just did). There's a reason 8 of the Oilers' 13 games have seen their opponents score two goals or fewer. And if they need to get into a foot race and match the other team's offense, they can do that too. They've already beaten both the worst and the best team in the league in run-and-gun games.\n\nThe Devils are definitely not just any team, but I still think they're being heavily overpriced here, unless something happened in NYC over the past two days that we're not aware of.\n\n𝐏𝐑𝐄𝐃𝐀𝐓𝐎𝐑𝐒 𝐌𝐋 +𝟏𝟕𝟐 (𝟎.𝟓𝐮)\nCarolina has been nearly unstoppable and hasn't missed a beat since winning the Cup. But sometimes, it's a random-ass team that catches a powerhouse off guard in a mid-week game. Nashville is exactly that kind of team. Nobody really knows where they stand, which makes them a tough team to prepare for. They're also an unusually veteran-heavy group, with aging players making up the core, and that can go either way on any given night. However, those players are still highly impactful, and some are even playing some of the best hockey of their recent careers. Even the acquisition of Shane Wright fits that \"unknown\" theme. This is exactly the type of game where the Hurricanes could get caught sleeping, much like the Avs did when they rolled into Nashville and got absolutely blown out just over a week ago."},"text":"𝑵𝑯𝑳 𝑷𝒍𝒂𝒚𝒔 𝒕𝒐𝒅𝒂𝒚, 𝑷𝒍𝒆𝒂𝒔𝒆 𝑹𝒆𝒂𝒅:\nPlease don't go big on any of these unless you see reasons otherwise. These are all pretty much value-lean shots. I'm hoping to catch some bad lines, but I know these could all lose. This includes my Jets collaboration play. https://t.co/npB7blckNt","url":"https://x.com/RazorsInsight/status/2117706508570124313"},{"article":{"title":"Every free sports pack from every top ranked handicapper for Tuesday"},"author_id":"14312093","created_at":"2026-11-03T17:04:57.000Z","edit_history_tweet_ids":["2117664340572512615"],"id":"2117664340572512615","text":"https://t.co/c5nnzh2BeW","url":"https://x.com/offshoreinsider/status/2117664340572512615"},{"author_id":"1774895006358081536","created_at":"2026-11-03T13:03:57.000Z","edit_history_tweet_ids":["2117603689137389929"],"id":"2117603689137389929","note_tweet":{"text":"☕ LAST NIGHT, GRADED\n102 games against bet105's closing lines. Here's everything.\n\n✅ Cover of the night: Illinois -39 (-117). Won by 75, 36 points clear. Fairleigh Dickinson 45, Illinois 120\n🐶 Dog of the night: Memphis +903 beat the Iowa State outright. Memphis 80, Iowa State 76\n💀 Bad beat: Suns +2.5, missed by 0.5. Suns 113, Warriors 116\n\n📊 THE BOARD\nFavorites